# Events / quiz domain security

- Participant registration captures PII (name, email, phone): collect minimum needed; show privacy notice when UI is built.
- One registration / one attempt per email per event unless product explicitly allows more.
- AI question generation: organizer-only; rate-limit; never trust model output without schema validation; strip/limit prompt injection from subject text.
- Correct answers and full answer keys: organizer-only endpoints.
- After registration deadline or capacity full: reject new registrations server-side (UI alone is not enough).
- Live quiz: authenticate participant session/token bound to `event_id` + `registration_id`.
- Do not leak whether an email is registered via distinct error messages on auth where enumeration matters — use generic messaging.
- Store all deadlines and timers in UTC; never trust the browser clock for eligibility or scoring.
- See `PROJECT.md` for flows, collections, and API contracts before inventing alternate schemas.
